@startuml doorbell-delivery
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

title Doorbell delivery modes

participant "Sender\n(terminal hook, main loop,\nwaggle message)" as R $AGENT
queue "Per-session inbox\n(host state)" as I $PRIVATE
participant "Doorbell router\n(session host)" as Pump $SERVICE
participant "Provider host\n(adapter)" as H $SERVICE
participant "Hosted session" as S $AGENT

== Today (fact) ==
R -> I: one durable notice per terminal run
Pump -> I: tick, or a nudge on attach
alt at least one client attached
  Pump -> H: deliver the coalesced text
  H -> S: Claude: bracketed paste\nCodex: turn/start (idle) or turn/steer (active)
else no client attached
  Pump -> Pump: keep the notices queued\nuntil the next attach
end

== Target (proposed, spec §7) ==
R -> I: message with a mode
Pump -> I: deliver whether or not a client is attached;\ncoalesce waiting messages
alt next_turn (default)
  Pump -> H: next_turn
  H -> S: idle: a new turn at once\nbusy: at the next turn boundary
else steer (where the harness supports it)
  Pump -> H: steer
  H -> S: Codex: turn/steer into the exact in-progress turn\nClaude: paste at a safe point, else next_turn
else interrupt (halt, park, emergency stop only)
  Pump -> H: interrupt
  H -> S: stop the running turn\n(Codex turn/interrupt; Claude interrupt key)
  H -> S: then deliver the message
end
H --> Pump: event: delivered, turn started
Pump --> R: event stream (main loop, waggle)

caption Sources: docs/claude-goal-runtime.md; internal/sessionmanager/manager_notice.go, codex_host.go, codex_context.go; waggle §10; spec §2.5, §7
@enduml
